        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?method=TopicQuote&TOPIC_ID=954&FORUM_ID=5&CAT_ID=2&Forum_Title=Infront+of+the+Fireplace&Topic_Title=A+note+to+Lore+Keepers"><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="#000000" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> *sitting infront of the fireplace, Abyn composes a journal entry in his tome*</P><P>I have and am part of a very good guild.  I sit here reminded of some words that one of our former guild members, has stated  on what makes Lore Keepers Different.</P><P>--<BR>  "I look at the e'ci boards and see a trend. Everyone posts whatever they want, trolls/anon posting But NOONE does what I see LK do. They respond to each others posts...Penitent posts and be sure Lady lling will too, Silverbeard will and Talil... That is unity, That is family. My idea of a friend? &lt; Six tough guys argueing with me in the street&gt;<BR>Tough guy #1<BR>"The sky is blue ya moron!"<BR>Me<BR>"The sky is RED you (*&!"</P><P>&lt;along comes Talil and Teggo&gt;</P><P>Teggo:<BR>"whats up?"<BR>me:<BR>"I'm telling this idiot the sky is red! tell em!"<BR>&lt;Talil and Teggo look to each other and /shrug and say&gt;</P><P>"Yeah he's right it IS RED ya *(&!"</P><P>In other words I can be TOTALLY wrong and they will back me up. Us against them. I see LK doing that for each other. Supporting one another in Posts, tells, /ooc /shout. It makes me very proud..."</P><P>-- Valimar</P><P>Even though members have come and gone, Lore Keepers still remain what it was.  I am very proud to be a member of a wonderous crew.  Even though our officers have dwindled some, but a core still remain, we are still under excellent leadership.  But as i have noted in the past, a guild is only as great as those who actively participate in it, and I must say we have a lot of active, participants and in that we will continue to be a great guild.</P><P></P><P></P><P>Edited by - abyn on 02 Apr 2001  19:28:48</font></td>
      </tr>

